<title>HUNGARY: German DBBH continues to buy Hungary MKB bank shrs.</title>
<headline>German DBBH continues to buy Hungary MKB bank shrs.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Deutsche Balaton Broker Holding AG (DBBH) will continue to buy series &quot;C&quot; preference shares of Hungary's Magyar Kulkereskedelmi Bank (MKB) although it closed an official purchase period.</p>
<p>DDBH released a statement through its Hungarian subsiadiary Elso Nemet Kft on Friday, saying it will continue to buy MKB shares at 35,000 forints, the price in the purchase period. Earlier on Friday, it said the period had ended as of May 30.</p>
<p>An Elso Nemet official told Reuters that DBBH would publish the price it offered for the shares in Hungarian daily Napi.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
